Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 14:45:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?phlink:=20phase=2006-06=20=E2=80=94=20network-s?=
 =?UTF-8?q?tate=20isolation=20per=20top-level=20site?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Per PRD §6 PRIV-06, phlink isolates network state per top-level site
so that cross-site loads cannot piggy-back on a peer site's cached
responses, V8 code cache entries, or open HTTP/socket connections.
Upstream Chromium ships these features `DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT` because
of cache-hit-rate regressions. phlink accepts the trade-off.

Flips, in net/base/features.cc:
- kSplitCacheByNetworkIsolationKey                 OFF → ON
- kSplitCodeCacheByNetworkIsolationKey             OFF → ON
- kPartitionConnectionsByNetworkIsolationKey       OFF → ON

`kSplitHostCacheByNetworkAnonymizationKey` and
`kThirdPartyStoragePartitioning` are already enabled upstream and
remain unchanged.

Refs PRD §6 (PRIV-06), plan 06-06.
---
 net/base/features.cc | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/base/features.cc b/net/base/features.cc
index 7c114ad0d084e..725b01900f0f5 100644
--- a/net/base/features.cc
+++ b/net/base/features.cc
@@ -125,14 +125,19 @@ const base::FeatureParam<base::TimeDelta>
 BASE_FEATURE(kSplitCacheByIncludeCredentials,
              base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
+// phlink (PRD §6 PRIV-06 / plan 06-06): partition the HTTP cache,
+// V8 code cache, and HTTP/socket connection pool per top-level site
+// so cross-site loads cannot piggy-back on a peer site's cached
+// responses or open connections. These default OFF upstream because
+// of cache-hit-rate regressions; phlink accepts that trade-off.
 BASE_FEATURE(kSplitCacheByNetworkIsolationKey,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kSplitCodeCacheByNetworkIsolationKey,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kPartitionConnectionsByNetworkIsolationKey,
-             base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+             base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kSplitHostCacheByNetworkAnonymizationKey,
              base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
